1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Sources==
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Primary===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/7107/37108/10 Christening Mar 16. 1879] - Domkirken parish, Bergen.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/314/2057/61 Marriage Oct 24. 1908] - Korskirken parish, Bergen
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Census===
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.digitalarkivet.no/nn/census/person/pf01053295005528 1885] - Claus Fastingsgade 33, Bergen
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.rhd.uit.no/folketellinger/ftliste.aspx?ft=1900&knr=1301&kenr=069&bnr=0029&lnr=03 1900] - Skudevigsveien 11, Bergen
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:X4JW-5TS 1930] - Brooklyn, NY, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Other===
2 CONT
2 CONT Sigvard was employed as a steward onboard the transatlantic ocean liner M/S Bergensfjord and is listed in Ellis Island records in [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:JX2X-TX9 1907], [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:JJ
2 CONC J6-S2L 1910] og [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:JNDV-3M5 1923]
2 CONT
2 CONT In [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:JJG8-62N 1911] his wife [http://www.libertyellisfoundation.org/passenger-details/czoxMjoiMTAxMjA1MTEwMjYwIjs=/czo5OiJwYXNzZW5nZXIiOw== Gudrun] arrives in US with their first born Sigrid.
2 CONT They were delayed as their transport, the RMS Olympic (sister vessel of Titanics), [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RMS_Olympic#Hawke_collision collided] with HMS Hawke near Isle of Wight Sept 20. Neither crew or passengers were kil
2 CONC led or badly injured. Olympic made it to Southampton, but was too damaged to continue the journey. Travellers were transferred to other vessels.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.myheritage.no/research/collection-10024/usa-statsborgerskapsregister?itemId=987458-&action=showRecord This] source state that Sigvard became a US citizen in 1930. Supported by [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/
2 CONC 1:1:XGND-J2F this] one.
2 CONT According to his family, which at the time had returned to Norway, Sigvard was struck by a meat hook while working in a meat locker, resulting in fatal head injuries. During their stays in US, the family lived in Brooklyn, hence o
2 CONC ne may assume this is where he was killed. However, excact location of his grave is unknown.
