1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Johan Garmann (1744–1810) was the son of district judge (sorenskriver) Johan Garmann (1717–1768) and Wenke Henriksdatter von der Lippe. Born 5 January 1744 at Mjelde in Haus parish (Osterøy), died 10 January 1810 i
2 CONC n Bergen, aged 66. Landowner (proprietær) — inherited Store Sandviken near Bergen and Mjelde farm in Haus parish from his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 16 May 1772 to Cecilie Katharine Kahrs (1752–1829), daughter of goldsmith Jens Ditmarsønn Kahrs of Bergen. The wedding took place at home on the farm, "in the house at N. Mjelda," by royal dispensation. This marriage is th
2 CONC e origin of the combined family name "Kahrs Garmann," carried on by later generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had 7 children, three of whom survived to have families of their own: Jens Kahrs Garmann (inherited Sandviken), Wenche Karine Garmann and Christopher Garmann (inherited Mjelde farm).
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Hopstock (1876), Sollied (1923), hanseater.no, "Boe" family history site.
